{"kind":"stack","id":"digestion-stack","title":"The digestive system: how our bodies use food","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#073642","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Mouth"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"The mouth breaks food into small pieces with the teeth and mixes it with saliva to start digestion."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"Which part of the body breaks food into small pieces using the teeth?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"The mouth","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"The stomach","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"The large intestine","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"What is the main job of the stomach?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"To store and churn food, breaking it down with acid","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"To absorb most of the water from food","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"To make the bile that helps us digest fats","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"Small intestine"},{"type":"text","id":"c4-e","content":"The small intestine finishes digesting food and absorbs the nutrients into the blood."},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Where are most nutrients from our food taken into the blood?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"The small intestine","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"The mouth","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"The oesophagus","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"What is the job of the oesophagus?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"To carry food from the mouth to the stomach","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"To remove waste from the body","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-c","label":"To make the enzymes that digest starch","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"You bite into a juicy apple. Your body starts digesting it straight away. What do you do next?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"Chew it slowly and mix it with saliva","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Swallow it in big lumps","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"Chewing breaks the apple into small pieces and saliva starts the digestion. The pieces travel down to the stomach smoothly."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"Big lumps are harder to digest. Your stomach has to work harder to break them down before the nutrients can be absorbed."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"What does saliva do when we eat?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"It starts breaking down food","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"It makes food hot","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"It removes waste from the body","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done! You finished the digestive system quiz."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Your body works hard every time you eat. Keep asking how things work!"}],"actions":[]}}
